# Monorepo layout: backend/ and (soon) frontend/ each have their own node_modules,
# build output and .env. None of the patterns below start with a slash, so git
# matches them at ANY depth — backend/.env and frontend/node_modules/ are already
# covered. Adding a leading slash to any of these would silently un-ignore the
# workspace copies, so don't.

# Environment — covers backend/.env, frontend/.env
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Dependencies — covers backend/node_modules/, frontend/node_modules/
node_modules/

# Build output — covers backend/dist/ (tsc) and frontend/dist/ (Vite)
dist/
build/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/

# Impeccable (design tooling) — installed per-developer, not part of the project.
#
# Unlike the patterns above, these contain a slash, which anchors them to this
# file's directory (the repo root). That is deliberate: it is exactly where the
# tool installs, and anchoring keeps them from matching anything a workspace
# might legitimately name the same way.
#
# The .github/ copies are NOT read by GitHub Actions — only workflows/ is. They
# are the GitHub Copilot install: Copilot reads repo-level hooks from
# .github/hooks/*.json, so committing that manifest would fire the design hook
# on every edit for anyone who clones this and uses Copilot, without them ever
# opting in. The consent that gates it is per-developer and local. The 3.5 MB
# skills/ tree it depends on is also a second copy that has already drifted from
# the .claude/ one actually in use here.
.github/agents/
.github/hooks/
.github/skills/

# Generated review output: screenshots (~0.5 MB a pass) and point-in-time
# critique scores, both regenerated every run and stale as soon as the code
# moves. .impeccable/design.json IS tracked — it is the token source the UI is
# built against, so the design system stays reproducible from the repo.
.impeccable/review/
.impeccable/critique/
.impeccable/questions/
.impeccable/config.local.json


CODE_GUIDE.MD